      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/corydoras-cf-urucu-2/",
      "html": "<p>The fish were collected in the surroundings of Labrina in the Rio Mucuim, in the central part of the Rio Purus. According to the exporters, very similar fish also occur in the Rio Urucu and Rio Jutai, both tributaries of the Solimões, but very far away from the Rio Mucuim.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/corydoras-cf-urucu-2/",
      "html": "<p>These catfish were imported as Corydoras evelynae, a species described from only one specimen with a very inaccurate locality (\"upper Solimões\", an area larger than Germany). Apart from the place of discovery, the fish are very similar to Corydoras urucu, which was described in 2009 from the river of the same name. However, C. urucu is said to be a dwarf species that should not grow larger than 2–3 cm, while the largest of these animals are well twice as big. Obviously, this is a species complex that needs to be explored in more detail.</p><p>The fish are very variable in pattern. Some animals are coloured similarly to C. evelynae and have a back band dissolved into dots, while the majority resemble Corydoras arcuatus in colour. However, the body shape is quite different from that of C. arcuatus and is more reminiscent of the relatives of C. loretoensis.</p>"
    }
  ],
